    "body": "This is a good question. Since serialization isn't actually going through indexed access on the TAs, we could serialize OOB ArrayBuffer views as is. The mental model I'm trying to perpetuate is \"being out of bounds behaves like being detached\", but as you point out it's a thing that can change over time, unlike being detached.\r\n\r\nI don't have too strong an opinion here. Outside of breaking consistency with my preferred mental model, I don't see any downsides to allowing them to be serialized. Do other folks have a preference?",
