    "body": "Discussed this internally with @marjakh. We're in favor keeping the OOB check here, because in normal JS code you cannot have OOB TypedArrays at creation time. So if we allow serialization of OOB TAs here, deserialization code will need to support being able to create OOB TypedArrays. This is extra complexity that doesn't seem worth it: in the limit you can imagine it being a security problem. The \"might go back into bounds later\" use case doesn't seem that compelling and seems more like a corner case.\r\n\r\nIf no strong feelings in allowing these, V8 would like to keep this PR as-is.",
    "created_at": "2022-11-29T14:06:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-29T14:06:47Z",
